From f5c2fdc3b0fe13d5d86a8535363e4daa5dae3786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 16:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inputd: keyboard layout at boot from KEYMAP= in cmdline.txt
 (#36)

inputd --keymap-boot [file] sets the layout named by KEYMAP= in the
environment or on the kernel command line, the devicetree /chosen
bootargs where the Raspberry Pi firmware puts cmdline.txt from the
card FAT partition, else the one in file (default /etc/keymap). The
unit 05_keymap runs it before the consoles start, so the layout of an
image is one word in a file on the card.

inputd --keymap prints the active layout: a read of the control handle
returns its name. orblogin can show it instead of assuming us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
